      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why BACKWARD_TRANSITIVE:  it is the only setting that lets us add message types (a new union branch is never forward-compatible);\ntransitive because events live for weeks, so a consumer must read data written by ANY schema still in retention;  it matches the command topic exactly\n(one consumer \u2014 us \u2014 upgrades first);  and its weak spot, old consumers reading new data, is covered by guards 1\u20133 above.",
      "originalText": "Why BACKWARD_TRANSITIVE:  it is the only setting that lets us add message types (a new union branch is never forward-compatible);\ntransitive because events live for weeks, so a consumer must read data written by ANY schema still in retention;  it matches the command topic exactly\n(one consumer \u2014 us \u2014 upgrades first);  and its weak spot, old consumers reading new data, is covered by guards 1\u20133 above.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
